{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KrshHHzhVLAP52dTrj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the pitch from your answers, at about 290 words.\n\n<final_document>\n**Bring Back the Majestic**\n\nThe Majestic on Main Street closed in 2022. Right up to the end it was selling about 180 tickets a week. Since then, the nearest cinema has been 38 miles away.\n\nWe want to reopen it, and this time we have a plan that can get there.\n\n**What we need**\n\nWe need $85,000 to replace the projector and sound system and to fix the roof.\n\n**Why this time is different**\n\nThree years ago we asked for $120,000. You pledged $47,000. It wasn't enough, so we gave every dollar back.\n\nSince then:\n\n- The building's owner has agreed to rent us the Majestic for $1 a year for ten years once we raise the money.\n- 46 volunteers have signed up to run the box office and the snack bar.\n- A local bank has pledged $25,000 if we raise the rest by June 30.\n- Three local businesses have pledged $11,000 in writing.\n\nThat leaves $49,000 to raise from the public. Last time, this town pledged $47,000.\n\n**If we fall short**\n\nThis is all-or-nothing. If we don't reach $85,000 by June 30, every pledge is returned in full, just like last time.\n\n**If we succeed**\n\nWe plan to reopen by Thanksgiving. Every three months we'll post a public report at the town library showing how every dollar was spent.\n\n**How you can help**\n\nPledge what you can by June 30. Then tell a neighbor, especially one who remembers a Friday night at the Majestic.\n\nWe're close enough this time to do it.\n\nRuth Albers\nChair, Majestic volunteer group\n</final_document>\n\nA few things to look at before it goes out:\n\n- **The $49,000 figure** is $85,000 minus the bank's $25,000 and the businesses' $11,000. I put it next to last time's $47,000 because that comparison is the strongest point you have. Please check that the businesses' $11,000 counts toward the total and isn't on top of it.\n- **The roof estimate could go up by as much as 15%.** I didn't put this in the pitch because I don't know what you'd do if it happens. If you have a plan, like a contingency or a cap, one line saying so would protect you later. The quarterly library reports partly cover this already.\n- **Things I left out because you don't know them yet:** why the cinema closed, a break-even budget, rewards, tax status and the bank's name. A pitch this short works without them. But the biggest question backers will have is \"won't it just close again?\", and a simple running-costs estimate would answer it.\n- **Films:** the pitch makes no promise about new releases or what will play.\n- **Your title:** \"Majestic volunteer group\" is a placeholder. Swap in your group's real name if it has one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":10241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1e552e0-f8c3-4ca7-8691-119fd8c80637","uuid":"d9557da1-e338-4b1e-a047-83a2d624232d","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:35:35.640Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KrsXsKG5z4NdTJcTpt"}
